  "report_discrepancies": [],
  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit, FYE 9/30/2022 (same structure as FY2023). Governmental lines from Exhibit E (Totals 2022 column, p4); Taxes 69,273 split into property tax 59,887 + motor vehicle tax 9,386 and Intergovernmental revenues 63,023 split into highway allocation, motor vehicle fees, municipal equalization aid, homestead allocation and other, using the Schedule 1 Totals 2022 column (p8), each adding up exactly. Capital outlay 47,293 (General 20,793 + Street 26,500) has no single printed function, so labelled 'Capital Outlay' on the statement line; in detail the Street Fund column gets Streets/Highways. Sale of properties 0 this year. Fund balances 529,952 + 266,833 - 187,946 + 15,730 - 85,689 = 538,880. Cash = cash in bank + cash with county treasurer from the governmental funds statement (p3; 2021 comparative column for the beginning); CDs as investments. Business-type (single proprietary column) from Exhibit H (p6), which ties to the Statement of Activities (expenses 230,866, charges 145,518, investment earnings 565, transfers 70,159 / (200), net position 496,360 -> 481,536, p2): 496,360 + 146,083 - 230,866 + 69,959 = 481,536. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1) because the governmental funds statement (538,880) does not equal governmental activities (capital assets, long-term debt); business-type cash in bank 0 omitted. Detail: Schedule 1 (per fund, p8) and Schedule 3 (proprietary, Actual column, p10; principal paid and purchase of capital assets are 0 in the Actual column); Schedule 2 (p9) is a combined budget summary (receipts 498,805 vs budget 413,018; disbursements 489,313 vs budget 1,149,000) with no line items, not recorded. Proprietary cash flow statement (p7) not recorded (cash basis, as FY2023). Read pages 1-10 of 10"
}
